// Inverse roach motel -- SOURCE program (access inside the critical section).
//
// rmm-zoo property: irm (Other local transformations / Inverse roach motel).
// Source: Poetzl & Kroening, "Formalizing and Checking Thread Refinement for
//         Data-Race-Free Execution Models" (arXiv:1510.07171, 2015), section 4.
//         The zoo notes this column is NOT from the Moiseenko et al. survey:
//         see models.json propertyProvenance["irm"].
//
// Roach motel reordering moves a shared access INTO a critical section (always
// sound where it holds). The inverse moves one OUT, weakening the synchronisation
// the access enjoys. Poetzl & Kroening prove this sound for the SC-for-DRF
// execution model; the zoo's irm column is 'yes' for exactly the SC-preserving /
// SC-for-DRF models and blank elsewhere -- including for MRD and sMRD, which is
// why MoRDor had no test for it.
//
// Here the read of x is inside the critical section; in opt.lit it has been
// hoisted above the lock.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  lock;
  r1 := x;
  y := 1;
  unlock
} ||| {
  lock;
  x := 1;
  unlock
}
